{{- /*
Arch and CachyOS ship Helix's binary as `helix` (/usr/bin/helix ->
/usr/lib/helix/hx) and provide no `hx`. Debian/Ubuntu -- including the
maveonair PPA this repo uses on Mint -- and the upstream release tarball
ship it as `hx`.

Every call site here says `hx`: EDITOR/VISUAL/ZK_EDITOR in .zshenv and
.bashrc, the `h`/`hz`/`hb` aliases, the note helpers in 55-notes.zsh, the
fzf opener in 40-fzf.zsh, and .config/helix/config.toml's hx-yazi bindings.
Rather than rewrite all of them per distro, put `hx` on PATH where the
distro omits it. Helix canonicalizes its own executable path, so going
through this symlink still finds /usr/lib/helix/runtime.

.chezmoiignore drops this target on non-Arch systems, where a real `hx`
already exists and this would shadow it.
*/ -}}
{{ if lookPath "helix" }}{{ lookPath "helix" }}{{ else }}/usr/bin/helix{{ end }}
